      "content": "thanks, i see what you mean about the subversion thing. but to be honest, that taco truck one feels a bit too \"safe\" and \"Disney\" for the crowd i'm playing. they want stuff that actually bites a little. \n\ninstead of trying to 'subvert' the tropes, i think i want to see if I can just lean into them more directly to see if the tension works. could we try some jokes that are a bit more blunt about the stereotypes? like, maybe something about the 'loud' or 'aggressive' perception people have, or even some jokes about the whole illegal immigration/crime angle? i just want to see where the actual edge is before i start writing the real stuff.",
